homelab-postfix (0.1.13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * behind_haproxy now defaults to TRUE (was false), per direction:
    the safe/recommended posture (matches production, stays correct
    whether this host ends up alone or split) should be the path of
    least resistance, not something you have to know to turn on.
    Bumped its debconf prompt to high priority (was medium) so a plain
    interactive install actually sees and understands it, and the
    postinst's final summary now states plainly whether this host
    expects HAProxy in front and what happens if it isn't there yet

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:26:26 -0500

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:07:29 -0500

homelab-postfix (0.1.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix a real bug in 0.1.11's smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol change,
    found via live testing (not assumed): setting it unconditionally
    does NOT degrade gracefully for a direct, non-proxied connection --
    confirmed it rejects every plain SMTP connection with "421 Server
    local error" (haproxy read: timeout error) while Postfix waits for
    a PROXY-protocol preamble that never arrives. Made it opt-in
    (homelab-postfix/behind_haproxy, default false, re-promptable via
    dpkg-reconfigure), same shape as homelab-dovecot's own
    behind_haproxy flag for the identical listener-level failure mode

homelab-postfix (0.1.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release v0.1.11

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 10:00:15 -0500

homelab-postfix (0.1.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Decouple from homelab-dovecot -- virtual_transport/smtpd_sasl_path
    now point at a configurable dovecot_host (debconf, default
    localhost) over plain TCP (LMTP:24, SASL auth:12345) instead of
    127.0.0.1/a local unix socket. Confirmed against this project's own
    production mail stack, which really runs Postfix and Dovecot on
    separate hosts this exact way. homelab-dovecot is now a Recommends,
    not a hard Depends
  * Removed the cross-package SASL drop-in this replaces (the
    postinst no longer writes into Dovecot's own conf.d/ at all, and
    the install-order dependency that required is gone with it) --
    homelab-dovecot now exposes its auth listener unconditionally on
    its own
  * Added smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol = haproxy (confirmed a real,
    global main.cf parameter via postconf -d) so this can sit behind
    homelab-haproxy with send-proxy -- harmless when not actually
    proxied

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:59:51 -0500

homelab-postfix (0.1.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Explicitly set inet_interfaces = all -- never set here before, it
    silently inherited whatever the underlying `postfix` package
    defaulted to for its own (never preseeded) debconf questions, which
    happened to be `all` on the one already-configured host this
    package had ever been installed on, but `loopback-only` on a
    genuinely fresh install. Confirmed live: this made SMTP/submission
    completely unreachable from any other host the first time this
    package was actually installed somewhere new -- an accidental
    correctness that greenfield/install-time testing was always going
    to eventually catch

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 23:07:43 -0500

